  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\n- $2{x}^{2}{y}^{\u2033}-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x\\,{y}^{\u2032}+{y}^{2}=0$\n- $2{y}^{\u2033}+{x}^{3}{y}^{\u2032}+2xy=0$\n- ${y}^{\u2033}+x{y}^{\u2032}=x{e}^{x}$",
  "worked_solution": "\u0410 second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{\u2033}+b(x){y}^{\u2032}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}{y}^{\u2033}-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x\\,{y}^{\u2032}+{y}^{2}=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term ${y}^{2}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{y}^{\u2033}+{x}^{3}{y}^{\u2032}+2xy=0\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=2,b(x)={x}^{3},c(x)=2x,$ and $f(x)=0.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}+x{y}^{\u2032}=x{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=1,b(x)=x,c(x)=0,$ and $f(x)=x{e}^{x}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
